"""Course content for the site: modules, concepts and the glossary. build.py turns it into pages.

Concept fields
  t      still time (s); its caption comes from stills/captions.json
  k      kicker (notebook section · year)
  title  heading
  one    the idea in one plain sentence, shown first
  bridge (title, HTML): "A familiar idea first", an ML-agnostic idea a developer already knows (loop tiling, a fold,
         a dict lookup, memoization …) that the explanation builds on. Shown before the body.
  body   the explanation (HTML). [[term]] or [[term|shown text]] links a glossary term (hover/tap definition)
  example a worked numeric example, after the body (optional)
  tex    the math, folded under "The math" (optional)
  era    "Back then": what people were struggling with (optional)
  biz    "The business side": the commercial stakes, such as cost, products and markets (optional)
  lore   memes, stories and jokes from the time (optional). Folklore is labeled as such.
  lab    notebook section

Lore rule: only stories that are documented; where an anecdote is folklore or its wording is disputed, say so.
"""

