                 bridge=('A valve instead of a dimmer', 'A sigmoid is a dimmer that never passes more than a quarter of a change through. ReLU is a valve: fully open for positive values, shut for negative ones. A row of open valves loses nothing.'),
                 biz='Cheap math matters at scale. ReLU is a single comparison, while a sigmoid needs an exponential. Across billions of activations per image, simpler operations mean faster, cheaper chips.',
