                 body="<p>Memory (1997), depth (2015), attention (2017), scale (2020): four claims, each a paper with a date. In practice [[baseline]] is the most useful word in this course. <strong>Before reaching for a large model, build the cheapest thing that could work and measure it on held-out data.</strong> On tabular data, gradient-boosted trees still often win.</p>",
                 era="Every era in this course believed it had found the answer, and every era was partly right. The parts that survived are the ones that scaled.",
